Steps:
[NAV] {{BACK_URL}}
[ACT] sign in as {{ADMIN_EMAIL}} / {{ADMIN_PASSWORD}}
[WAIT] platform main menu loaded
[ACT] open the "Sales Reps" app from the main menu (embedded VC-Shell app, route #!/workspace/embedded-app/vc-sales-rep)
[WAIT] Sales Reps list (data-test SalesRepsList) loaded
[GRID] read the reps grid rows

Assertions:
[GRID] SR_REP_PRIMARY (@td(SR_REP_PRIMARY.email)) appears exactly once in the list {OBSERVED}
[GRID] a rep whose sales-rep:access comes only from a per-org membership role also appears — the list is the union of the global-role and per-org-role sources {OBSERVED}
[GRID] no user appears twice — the union is deduped by user {OBSERVED}
[DOM] verify whether a user who holds no role granting sales-rep:access is absent from the list {HYPOTHESIS}

Cross_Layer_Checks:
[API] the reps search (POST /api/sales-rep/search) resolves membership by the sales-rep:access permission, NOT by a fixed role id/name {SPEC}
[CONSOLE] no JS errors while the list loads {OBSERVED}
[NETWORK] no 4xx/5xx on the reps search request {OBSERVED}

Assertions:
[GRID] @td(SR_REP_NOCUSTOMERS.email) is present in the list — a rep with the global role but no served orgs still counts as a rep {OBSERVED}
[GRID] its Organizations column reads 0 (zero served orgs) {OBSERVED}
[DOM] verify whether the "Not assigned Sales Reps" filtered view lists this rep once implemented (currently a coming-soon stub) {HYPOTHESIS}

[DOM] Save succeeds and the blade transitions back to the list {OBSERVED}
[GRID] the new rep (AGENT-TEST-sr-admNNN@example.com) appears in the reps list {OBSERVED}
[FORM] reopening the rep shows the saved First/Last name, Email (login), Sales Rep role, and @td(ORG_ACME.id) under Served organizations {OBSERVED}

Cross_Layer_Checks:
[API] the create request (POST /api/sales-rep) returns 200; a Contact member AND a login ApplicationUser are both created (save order: member incl. Organizations -> account -> memberships) {OBSERVED}
[ADMIN] the login account exists in Platform > Security > Users with UserName = the login email {OBSERVED}
[CONSOLE] no JS errors during save {OBSERVED}

Assertions:
[FORM] the rep's GLOBAL account role equals the role selected in the create blade (Security > Users > Roles, count 1) {OBSERVED}
[STATE] the selected role grants sales-rep:access (role description "Grants Sales Rep access (sales-rep:access)") {OBSERVED}
[FORM] the same role is applied as the PER-ORG membership role for @td(ORG_ACME.id) (single "Sales Rep role" dropdown applies both, per help text) {SPEC}

[FORM] @td(ORG_ACME.id) appears under "Organizations served as Sales Rep" in the sales-rep app {OBSERVED}
[FORM] @td(ORG_ACME.id) appears under "Member of company(ies)" on the Contact (Contact.Organizations -> MemberRelation) {OBSERVED}
[STATE] a corresponding CustomerOrganizationMembership with a role granting sales-rep:access also exists (backend second write; both are required) {SPEC}

[DOM] the "Add" (create) action is not available to a user lacking platform:security:create — the toolbar exposes only "Refresh" (no Add/Delete) {OBSERVED}
[STATE] no rep member and no login account can be created by this user {OBSERVED}
[STATE] no orphan member/account is left behind {OBSERVED}

[DOM] every role offered grants sales-rep:access {OBSERVED}
[DOM] a role that does NOT grant sales-rep:access is NOT offered (dropdown showed exactly the 2 granting roles, not the full platform role list) {OBSERVED}
[DOM] a custom role that grants sales-rep:access IS offered — detection is by permission, not by the default role id/name {OBSERVED}

[FORM] the rep's GLOBAL account role is now R2 (re-pointed; Security > Users > Roles shows only R2, count 1) {OBSERVED}
[STATE] R1 (the previously granting role) is no longer assigned globally — other granting roles are stripped {OBSERVED}
[FORM] the PER-ORG membership role in @td(ORG_ACME.id) is likewise re-pointed to R2 (single dropdown applies both) {SPEC}

[GRID] reps holding sales-rep:access via the custom role are still detected and listed {SPEC}
[DOM] the "Sales Rep role" dropdown now offers the custom role (and no longer the deleted default) {SPEC}
[DOM] verify whether the default seeded role is re-created on the next app load — it must NOT be re-seeded while another role grants the permission {HYPOTHESIS}

[FORM] the saved Email (login) is the new value and it is first in the email list {OBSERVED}
[FORM] the duplicate additional email was de-duplicated (the login is not repeated in Additional emails; only the distinct extra remains) {OBSERVED}
[ADMIN] the account UserName equals the new login email (kept in sync) {OBSERVED}
[STATE] verify whether signing in with the new login email succeeds (login moved) {HYPOTHESIS}

[GRID] the rep no longer appears in the Sales Reps list {OBSERVED}
[ADMIN] the login account is GONE from Platform > Security > Users (0 results — no orphan account) {OBSERVED}
[STATE] the rep's roles and org memberships are also removed {OBSERVED}
